library for references - including the add-on's own app surfaces, not just the platform's. The agent library is both a bench plugin AND a standalone app (/agent/index.html, boot control agent.agent): a control retired from the bench story may still be load-bearing in the app story.\",\n    \"detail\": \"The incident: retiring the agentmodules cluster after checking only dev/app broke the Agent app's boot (it installed the cluster to build its module world) and the chat control (it called store.listTools, deleted from app.store in the same rework). Fix: the app boot installs agentloop/agentprompt/memory directly; chat rides agentloop.listTools. Also the disposable-instance recipe for testing published apps: runtime/<app>/app.properties (copy from data/<lib>/_APPS/<app>/app.properties) AND runtime/<app>/src (copy of _APPS/<app>/src) - do_get serves app pages from runtime/<app>/html/ then runtime/<app>/src/html/<app>/.\",\n    \"tags\": \"workflow,deletion,references,agent-app,disposable,runtime\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"regression found by the owner on his live instance + fixed and browser-verified, session 2026-08-10, branch claude/newbound-missing-library-fixes-bx9bs0 (agent.agent, agent.chat, agent.memory)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786372830834\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The bench-graft collapse's leaf pass is done on branch claude/app-loader-control-oa4cyw: dev.toast, dev.card, dev.jump, dev.session and app.sceneplayer are stock-dialect controls.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Recipe proven: ES-module body becomes the api-object constructor body; host->ME (document.getElementById(me.UUID)); props->ME.DATA (functions survive, installControl stores DATA by reference); exported api -> me.* methods; async setup queues behind a readyP promise with waitReady(cb) for embedders (sceneplayer). Verified on a disposable instance with Playwright: all five mount via installControl and exercise real store calls. /dev/ is BROKEN on this branch until the container pass (frame/workbench/editors/shelf/preview still mount via app.loader). Remaining: container pass, peer viewer off player/bridge, delete loader/bridge/player, shrink the dev boot.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786399738623\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The bench-graft container pass is done on branch claude/app-loader-control-oa4cyw: all eight dev containers (frame, shelf, workbench, editor, preview, floweditor, sceneeditor, floweditor3d) and the dev.dev boot are stock; /dev/ verified end-to-end headless with zero console errors.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Uniform wrapper: async prelude awaits requireModule deps + page-relative vendor dynamic imports, original body unchanged, init(ME, ME.DATA), api Object.assign'd onto me plus waitReady(cb). Child mounts via a local mount(name, el, props) helper over installControl honoring waitReady, child library explicit. dev.session html carries the classic dev:plugins div (replaces the loader's per-mount plugin pass); the boot keeps only the dev.dev-target plugin pass and mounts dev.frame stock. app.modules no longer installs loader. Remaining graft: delete app.loader/bridge/player + migrate the peer viewer (deletion pass), and convert agent.agent/agent.chat in the agent repo (they still build __benchPlatform).\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786401039404\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Bench collapse complete in both repos: dev IDE, peer viewer, and the agent app (chat/askrow/describebtn/agentloop/agentprompt/memory) all run stock; /dev/, /peer/ and /agent/ verified headless with zero console errors.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Library ready-ordering rule: a library control defines its global in me.ready and lists its own library deps as child divs; api.js activation guarantees children's readys before the parent's, transitively — so consumers gate their init on me.ready (readyP = new Promise(res => me.ready = res)). Remaining vestige: dev.code.set_module_flag (newbound_core-rooted, needs host rebuild to delete — left for a platform-side cleanup on a session without the overlay initializer entanglement). Known follow-up: /agent/ serving requires runtime/agent scaffold (publishapp output) — clone-fresh instances need the _APPS/agent copy, same as the disposable recipe's metaidentity seeding.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786403684763\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Both app boots are pure markup: dev.dev html = a dev:plugins div plus a stock dev:frame div (js facet empty; the control keeps its compile/rebuild commands); agent.agent html = one agent:chat div.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Boot-level plugin registry entries must name a selector — the hidden-holder fallback died with the imperative boot. The entire page load is api.js default activation: shell index.js activateControls(document) -> body data-control -> nested divs all the way down.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786405099434\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The bench collapse is MERGED TO MASTER in both repos (2026-08-11, owner-approved): the client platform is api.js alone, boots are markup, author defaults server-side, and the stale-world narration is swept from comments and UI strings.\",\n    \"detail\": \"agent.bench (the 250ms graft-slot poller) is deleted — its selectorless dev.dev registry entry died with the imperative boot. Live instances should retarget their plugin registry: askrow -> dev.session / .ss-plugins, describebtn -> dev.workbench / .wb-plugins (both hosts now carry the classic dev:plugins div), and drop the agent-bench entry. Hash routes (#/bench/...) and localStorage keys (bench.*) deliberately keep their historical names — renaming would break behavior and lose user state.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786407391814\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\"